# UST.G3CS: Selected Pole-Six Preimage First-Jet Theorem

## Statement

At the selected `GF(11)`, `gamma=3`, `a=0` proof fiber, write the exact
pole-six reduction of the fixed selected source numerator as

```text
N = J(a) h(a).
```

The G3CN first-jet coordinates split into quotient and image parts.  UST.G3CQ
and UST.G3CR closed the quotient-defect correction, but that correction is not
the complete derivative of `h`.

This theorem composes all 3,758,824 image-coordinate jet entries touched by the
117 nonzero selected `LS_j` multipliers.  After 19,878,831 sparse term products
are collected, the image contribution has 62,034 terms.  Adding the G3CQ
quotient correction gives ten original-partial rows with 60,708 terms.

The resulting `h'(0)` satisfies the exact differentiated identity

```text
J'(0) h(0) + J(0) h'(0) = 0.
```

Its independently replayed minus divergence has 11,236 ambient H02 terms and
a 217-coordinate B103 H02 normal form.

## Consequence

The selected pole-six preimage derivative is now complete at the proof fiber.
The quotient-defect correction alone must not be substituted for it.  The
emitted H02 ambient row is the correct input to the differentiated lower-pole
coordinate equations in UST.G3CT.

This theorem does not emit the full `1509 x 1509` operator derivative, perform
characteristic-zero path integration, or determine an integral period or
`beta_C`.

